(SECTION 8 - DUAL ENGINE FAILURE & RELIGHT) Tj T* T*
(8.2 DUAL ENGINE FLAMEOUT / RELIGHT PROCEDURE) Tj T*
T*
(CONDITION: Sudden loss of thrust on all engines at cruising altitude.) Tj T*
T*
(IMMEDIATE MEMORY ITEMS:) Tj T*
(1. Airspeed: Establish and maintain 270 KIAS optimum glide speed / windmill relight speed.) Tj T*
(2. APU \(Auxiliary Power Unit\): START switch to ON. Verify APU generator online within 60 seconds.) Tj T*
(3. RAT \(Ram Air Turbine\): Manual deploy handle PULL if electrical emergency bus not automatically powered.) Tj T*
(4. Engine Start Switches: Set to CONT \(Continuous Ignition\).) Tj T*
(5. Thrust Levers: Retard to IDLE to prevent fuel pooling during restart cycle.) Tj T*
(6. Crew Coordination: Notify ATC via Mayday broadcast on 121.5 MHz; Squawk 7700.) Tj T*
(7. Altitude: Determine glide distance to nearest suitable runway \(approx 2.5 NM per 1,000 ft altitude lost\).) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
