(SECTION 2 - EMERGENCY DESCENT PROCEDURES) Tj T* T*
(2.4 RAPID CABIN DEPRESSURIZATION & EMERGENCY DESCENT) Tj T*
T*
(CONDITION: Cabin altitude exceeds 10,000 feet or CABIN ALTITUDE WARNING alert illuminates.) Tj T*
T*
(CREW IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:) Tj T*
(1. Oxygen Masks: DON, Set 100% and Emergency Flow.) Tj T*
(2. Crew Communications: Establish interphone communication through mask microphones.) Tj T*
(3. Flight Controls: Initiate immediate emergency descent.) Tj T*
(   - Autopilot: DISENGAGE or select FLCH / OPEN DESCENT.) Tj T*
(   - Thrust Levers: IDLE.) Tj T*
(   - Speedbrake: EXTEND fully.) Tj T*
(   - Target Altitude: Descend immediately to 10,000 feet MSL or Minimum Enroute IFR Altitude \(MEA\), whichever is higher.) Tj T*
(4. Passenger Oxygen: Verify passenger oxygen masks deployed \(overhead switch OVERRIDE\).) Tj T*
(5. Transponder: Select SQUAWK 7700 on ATC transponder.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
