(SECTION 13 - HYDRAULIC SYSTEMS) Tj T* T*
(13.3 HYDRAULIC SYSTEM B LEAK / LOW PRESSURE) Tj T*
T*
(CONDITION: Hydraulic System B reservoir quantity below 10% and low pressure warning active.) Tj T*
T*
(OPERATIONAL IMPACT:) Tj T*
(Normal landing gear extension may be inoperative. Alternate gear extension via gravity drop will be required.) Tj T*
(Inboard flight spoilers and left thrust reverser may have degraded response times.) Tj T*
T*
(PROCEDURES:) Tj T*
(1. Hydraulic Pump B: Switch to OFF to prevent pump cavitation and thermal damage.) Tj T*
(2. Flaps / Slats: Plan approach using Flap 20 or designated abnormal configuration.) Tj T*
(3. Approach Speed: Compute VREF + 20 knots additive for degraded spoiler braking.) Tj T*
(4. Landing Distance: Multiply dry runway landing distance by factor of 1.45.) Tj T*
(5. Nose Wheel Steering: System B loss causes loss of normal nosewheel steering; plan towing off runway after rollout.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
